  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In parallelogram \\(ABCD\\), \\(AC=6\\), \\(BD=8\\), and \\(AB=5\\). Find the area of parallelogram \\(ABCD\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "24",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Let \\(O\\) be the intersection of diagonals \\(AC\\) and \\(BD\\). A parallelogram's diagonals bisect each other, so \\(OA=3\\), \\(OB=4\\), and \\(AB=5\\), satisfying \\(3^2+4^2=5^2\\). By the converse of the Pythagorean theorem, \\(\\angle AOB=90^\\circ\\). Thus, \\(AC\\perp BD\\), so \\(ABCD\\) is a rhombus. Its area is \\(6\\times8\\div2=24\\).",
